His Body will be conveyed from his house with a multi-racial pallbearers to the Capitol to lay in state at the United States Capitol rotunda. Only Clay and Lincoln have ever recieved this privledge and his is the first to be have the guard of honor be comprised of entirely Black soldiers.

May he rest in piece.

The Detroit Post: {!<cite>"if to die crowned with noble laurels, and ... secure of [recte in] the respect of the world ... is an end worthy the ambition of a well spent life, then the veteran Radical may lie down with the noblest of the fathers to a well contented sleep."<cite>!}

New York Times: {!<cite>"discerned the expediency of emancipation, and urged it long before Mr. Lincoln issued his proclamation" but that after the war, "on the subject of Reconstruction, then, Mr. Stevens must be deemed the Evil Genius of the Republican Party.<cite>!}